# docs/NATIVE-AGENTS.md §6.2 — the decision drawer's options are buttons that dispatch the same
#   action as their keys, and the composer's Send is the pointer's `⏎`
# docs/TESTING-HARNESS.md §3 — `agents.send`, `agents.approval.deny`, `agents.row[N]`, `agents.tool[N]`
#
# The same file-change gate the keyboard scenarios answer, driven by the pointer end to end:
# the prompt is sent with the Send button, the gate is denied with its Deny button, and the
# settled transcript's tool row is hovered and right-clicked for its verbs.
fixture: agents
await idle
key o
await screen == Workspace 20000

key ctrl-s A
await agents.threads[0].provider == codex 20000
# The summary can land before the create answer that selects the tab, so wait for the focus.
await focused == agents.composer 20000
await idle 30000
click agents.composer
type apply the README fix
click agents.send

await agents.threads[0].pending_gate == permission 30000
await agents.threads[0].state == needs_you 30000
assert key_contexts[2] == AgentPermission
shot approval

# Deny, by pointer. Codex's decline does not interrupt the turn, so it settles on its own.
click agents.approval.deny
await agents.threads[0].pending_gate absent 30000
assert agents.threads[0].state != needs_you
await agents.threads[0].state == idle 30000
assert sticky_error absent
shot settled

# The settled turn folds its one tool call into a group, `agents.row[2]` under the prompt and
# the first paragraph. A click opens it, so the call is a row of its own: `agents.tool[3]`.
click agents.row[2]
dump expanded
# The tool row's verbs show under the pointer, and its right-click menu carries the same ones.
hover agents.tool[3] 300
shot tool-hover
click right agents.tool[3]
shot tool-menu
key escape
# A click on the line itself toggles the row, as `⏎` does on the focused row.
click agents.tool[3]
shot tool-open
quit
